<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18446" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flūmĭnĕus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i>, <i>in</i>, or <i>belonging
				to a river</i>, <i>river</i>- (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 46</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					M. 14, 599</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">15, 565</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ulva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 5, 519</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ulmus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. Th.
					9</span></i>
			, 
			 266: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alnus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 458</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cygnus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					8, 67</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volucres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					2, 253</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">classis,</span>”
				<i>used for crossing a river</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					4, 494</span></i>
			.</div>
